Invented lists from release notes, changelogs and project READMEs, labeled by hand; no labeling round has read them.
A list where one opening word starts most items. Each case is a whole list. The hits run from 4 of 5 to 9 of 12;
the passes hold short lists, numbered steps, article openers and lists where the top word starts 3 of 5 or 4 of 6.
